<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Rahim of Bukhara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1758">1758</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Rahim of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> was a chief of the Manghit tribe who took effective power in the Khanate of Bukhara in the 1740s under the protection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>. After Nader's death in 1747 he pushed aside the Janid khans and in 1756 took the title of khan himself. His relatives continued Manghit rule, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-murad">Shah Murad</a> formalised as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Bukhara in 1785.</p></div>
